### F4a - E2E: DLM data round-trip (runtime-filled buffer + checksum)
- Fixture (no linker-script changes - raw pointers): QEMU phase first ENABLES
  the TCM (csr write milmb/mdlmb EN=1 -- required: vsim RTL resets EN=0, and
  the CSR write is what arms the write-mask restore), then loops a
  runtime-COMPUTED pattern into `(uint32_t*)0x200000` (hart-local DLM). ROI
  (vsim) reads the buffer back, checksums, prints `SUM=xxxxxxxx`; exit 0 iff
  SUM == precomputed EXPECTED.
- Why this is decisive: the bytes exist NOWHERE except the DLM (not in the ELF -
  runtime-computed; not in DRAM - the store went to the overlay; vsim loads no
  ELF content in hybrid). The ONLY road to a correct SUM is the handoff.
- Negative control for free: this fixture FAILS today (vsim DLM empty -> SUM
  wrong) and turns green when F1-F3 land - it IS the RED test for the feature.
- Assert in the harness: fixture image end < `0x200000` (R3).
- Key files: `tests/fixtures/rt_c_dlm_data.c`, `tests/fixtures/Makefile`,
  `vsim: cmake/HybridConfig.cmake` (e2e registration), `tests/e2e.sh` if needed
- Deps: F3

### F4b - E2E: ILM code round-trip (asm blob executed from TCM)
- Fixture: a small SELF-CONTAINED asm routine (`a0 = f(a0)`, no DRAM
  relocations) carried as a data blob in DRAM. QEMU phase copies it to
  hart-local ILM base+`0x100` (avoid NULL), `fence.i`, then ROI. ROI (vsim)
  calls the function pointer at `0x100` - the fetch comes from the ILM RTL -
  and checks the return value.
- Loud failure mode: an empty ILM fetches all-zero words = RISC-V illegal
  instruction -> traps inside the trap-free ROI (visible crash), on top of the
  return-value mismatch.
- Optional strengthening: patch an immediate inside the copied code with a
  runtime value (+ `fence.i`) so the result depends on exact instruction bytes.
- Cycle sanity (soft): DRAM-resident twin of the same kernel; expect
  cycles(ILM) < cycles(DRAM twin). Wide threshold - a sanity check, not a perf
  regression test.
- Key files: `tests/fixtures/rt_c_ilm_code.c` (+ inline `.word` blob),
  `tests/fixtures/Makefile`, `vsim: cmake/HybridConfig.cmake`
- Deps: F4a (reuses its harness plumbing)

